# Presence of this file makes porting-sdk/scripts/diff_port_signatures.py pass
# --defaults-ceiling for this port (auto-detected beside port_signatures.json,
# mirroring .drift-numeric-monotype).
#
# Go has no default-argument syntax. There is no `func f(x int = 5)`, so for the
# majority of parameters "what is this parameter's default" has no answer to
# record — the ABSENCE of a default is the truth, not a gap in the enumerator.
# Without this declaration those unrecorded defaults read as a 66.4% coverage
# HOLE (368 member params, 267 construction params) rather than the language
# ceiling they actually are.
#
# What the ceiling does and does not do:
#   * `default-mismatch` / `default-invented` drift is demoted to EXCUSED —
#     still counted and printed, never silently dropped, so the ceiling cannot
#     quietly widen.
#   * `required-flip` is NOT affected. Every language can express "the caller
#     must supply this", so a required flip is a real finding whether or not a
#     default is expressible. (Verified in diff_port_signatures.py: only drift
#     kinds with the `default-` prefix are demoted.)
#
# The enumerator still recovers a default wherever Go genuinely gives a caller
# an omittable argument — a sentinel guard (`if n <= 0 { n = 900 }`) or a
# zero-length variadic fallback — so the ceiling covers only what Go cannot
# express, not what this port has not bothered to enumerate. See the PARAMETER
# DEFAULT VALUES and PARAMETER OPTIONALITY blocks in
# cmd/enumerate-signatures/main.go.
